(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #108 aliasing probe: `orig` is a function argument -
 a retaining position, since the callee's parameter is a copy of the same
 pointer and can stash it anywhere reachable after the call returns (here,
 a global). The caller's later `Set orig to ...` must not free the string
 the callee is still holding onto through `kept`.)

a text called kept is "".

To 'keep' with a text called s.
    Set kept to s.

a number called n is 5.
a text called orig is "{n}".
'keep' with orig.
Set orig to "changed".
Print kept.
